From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:52:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(devices): pin views projection truncation at output
 capacity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

### What
Pins `DeviceRegistry::views` truncation: with more assigned devices than output slots, exactly the first `output.len()` views are projected in assignment order and the returned count is capped; a zero-length output projects nothing.

### Why it matters
The projection writes into a caller-fixed buffer. The existing test uses an output larger than the assignment set, so removing or weakening the capacity break survives the suite — and would index past the buffer.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| remove `count == output.len()` break | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `count == output.len()` -> `count > output.len()` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-devices --lib views_truncate`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs
index 887a25bd..6e11c291 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-devices/src/lib.rs
@@ -824,4 +824,33 @@ mod tests {
         net.close();
         assert_eq!(net.receive(&mut [0; 8]), Err(DeviceError::Closed));
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn views_truncate_to_output_capacity_without_overflow() {
+        let mut registry: DeviceRegistry<8, 8> = DeviceRegistry::new();
+        for i in 0..4u64 {
+            let name = [b'a' + i as u8; 4];
+            registry
+                .assign(1, 10 + i, DeviceName::new(&name).unwrap(), DeviceKind::Null)
+                .unwrap();
+        }
+        // capacity 2: only first two projected, count capped at capacity
+        let pad = DeviceView {
+            name: DeviceName::new(b"pad").unwrap(),
+            kind: DeviceKind::Null,
+            major: 0,
+            minor: 0,
+        };
+        let mut small = [pad; 2];
+        assert_eq!(registry.views(1, &mut small), 2);
+        assert_eq!(small[0].name.as_bytes(), b"aaaa");
+        assert_eq!(small[1].name.as_bytes(), b"bbbb");
+        // zero capacity projects nothing
+        let mut none: [DeviceView; 0] = [];
+        assert_eq!(registry.views(1, &mut none), 0);
+        // full capacity sees all four in assignment order
+        let mut full = [pad; 4];
+        assert_eq!(registry.views(1, &mut full), 4);
+        assert_eq!(full[3].name.as_bytes(), b"dddd");
+    }
 }
